    "Qoheleth"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "So I returned, and considered all the oppressions that are done under the sun: and behold the tears of such as were oppressed, and they had no comforter; and on the side of their oppressors there was power; but they had no comforter.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Wherefore I praised the dead which are already dead more than the living which are yet alive.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Yea, better is he than both they, which hath not yet been, who hath not seen the evil work that is done under the sun.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Again, I considered all travail, and every right work, that for this a man is envied of his neighbour. This is also vanity and vexation of spirit.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "The fool foldeth his hands together, and eateth his own flesh.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Better is an handful with quietness, than both the hands full with travail and vexation of spirit.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Then I returned, and I saw vanity under the sun.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "There is one alone, and there is not a second; yea, he hath neither child nor brother: yet is there no end of all his labour; neither is his eye satisfied with riches; neither saith he, For whom do I labour, and bereave my soul of good? This is also vanity, yea, it is a sore travail.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Two are better than one; because they have a good reward for their labour.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "For if they fall, the one will lift up his fellow: but woe to him that is alone when he falleth; for he hath not another to help him up.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Again, if two lie together, then they have heat: but how can one be warm alone?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "And if one prevail against him, two shall withstand him; and a threefold cord is not quickly broken.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Better is a poor and a wise child than an old and foolish king, who will no more be admonished.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "For out of prison he cometh to reign; whereas also he that is born in his kingdom becometh poor.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "I considered all the living which walk under the sun, with the second child that shall stand up in his stead.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "There is no end of all the people, even of all that have been before them: they also that come after shall not rejoice in him. Surely this also is vanity and vexation of spirit.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:4:16"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
